# Pairs with RAllOrNothing. The cross-tree receiver barrier decides as soon as
# ANY wait-set tree has arrived instead of every one, and takes its verdict
# over the trees that have arrived, so the first tree to report finalises both
# trees while the other tree's prepare may still be in flight: one tree serves
# the saga post-saga, the other pre-saga. Waiting for the whole wait set is the
# barrier's entire job.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingBarrierDecidesOnFirstTree
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the cross-tree receiver barrier decides on its first arrival rather than on the whole wait set
PERTURBS: ReceiverNotify

--- FIND
           complete == \A w \in live : eff[w] # "none"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: one arrival completes the barrier.
           complete == \E w \in live : eff[w] # "none"
--- END
--- FIND
             THEN /\ cdec' = IF \A w \in live : eff[w] = "committed" THEN "committed" ELSE "aborted"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the verdict is taken over the trees that have arrived.
             THEN /\ cdec' = IF \A w \in live : eff[w] \in {"none", "committed"} THEN "committed" ELSE "aborted"
--- END
